# Copy this file to ".env", adjust it, then: ./scripts/fetch-media.sh && docker compose up -d --build
#
# ── Where the app is reached ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Passkeys are bound to the exact hostname and only work over HTTPS (localhost is the
# one exception). For a quick try on the machine running Docker, keep these and open
# http://localhost:8080
RP_ID=localhost
ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080
WEB_PORT=8080
RP_NAME=openGym
#
# For a real deployment, put openGym behind something that serves HTTPS for your
# hostname (a reverse proxy, Cloudflare Tunnel, `tailscale serve`...) pointing at
# WEB_PORT, then set:
#
#   RP_ID=gym.example.com
#   ORIGIN=https://gym.example.com

# ── AI coach (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uses a Claude subscription, no API key. On a trusted computer with Claude Code
# installed run `claude setup-token` and paste the value here. At startup the server
# stores it encrypted in ./data and turns the coach on; each profile still has to
# accept it once in the Coach tab. Leave empty to keep the coach off.
#
#   CLAUDE_SETUP_TOKEN=
#
# Kill switch: forces the coach off whatever is stored.
#
#   COACH_DISABLED=1

# ── Sign-in length (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Days a sign-in lasts. Default 90.
#
#   SESSION_DAYS=90
